{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfe1sRYngvjJzphKUYVMw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I submitted a portfolio of the 10 signals with the largest absolute training Sharpe, each traded in its training-profitable direction and weighted by that Sharpe. It had a training Sharpe of 1.39 and a validation Sharpe of 0.30, and I did not try to push the validation number higher.\n\nLarger baskets had higher training Sharpe but lower validation Sharpe: 2.34 in training and 0.04 in validation for all 423 signals. That pattern means the training edge mostly doesn't carry over to 2000–2012. I used only five backtests, and the choice of 10 over larger baskets was informed by validation, so 0.30 is a modestly optimistic estimate of out-of-sample performance. I stopped there because searching further against validation would mostly fit noise rather than find a real edge."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":297,"cache_read_input_tokens":7489,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":297},"output_tokens":264,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5332db3d-4f98-41d1-9407-239a1b735b07","uuid":"248b634c-eff1-41b9-998b-1f01f5ee7b17","timestamp":"2026-10-02T20:08:51.247Z","request_id":"req_011Cfe1sRFvPiBnVvDyh4vuk"}
